
1.Basic Locators -> id, name, Linktext, Partial LinkText, ClassName, TagName
2.Customized Locators ->1. CSS Selector [Tag and ID, Tag and Class, Tag and Attribute, Tage, class and Attribute]
                      2. Xpath [Absolute Xpath, Relative Xpath ]


3.These are used to locate single webElement ->
a.id
b.name
c.linkText
d.partialLinkText

Tablets  Table -linkText()
Submit   Send  -partialLinkText()

4.These are used to locate mulitple webElement and group of webElement ->
Ex:total numbers of links, images, element in this page, for count or validate using these two locators.
a.TagName
b.Class

5.findElement() -> find the return single webElement,
6.findElements() -> find the return multiple webElement,
diff
scenario 1. locator matching with single webElement
findElement(loc) --> single webElement -> return WebElement
findElements(loc)--> single webElement -> return List<WebElement>

scenario 2. Locator is matching with multi webElements
findElement(loc)  ->single webElement at first locator-> return WebElement
findElements(loc) ->multiple webElement ->return List<WebElement>

scenario 3. locator is not matching with any element/s
findElement() -> return "No Such Element Exception "
findElements() -> will not throw any expection. Returns 0.